Subject: [PATCH] AccessibilityInputFilter: key events are filtered whatever display they carry

Ayaneo Pocket DS: the keys carry the focused display (the bottom screen when it has the focus), but
the accessibility input filter only has a handler for the default display and, with
ignoreInputEventsFromDisplayWithoutHandler, let every event of another display through unfiltered.
Accessibility services therefore never saw the keys while the bottom screen had the focus: the M
button of AYAHome (an accessibility service, key 190) did nothing then and worked with the focus on
the main screen. Key events all go through the KeyboardInterceptor of the default display anyway
(processKeyEvent), so they are no longer dropped for lack of a handler for their display.

diff --git a/services/accessibility/java/com/android/server/accessibility/AccessibilityInputFilter.java b/services/accessibility/java/com/android/server/accessibility/AccessibilityInputFilter.java
index f529b23f6..50f5096df 100644
--- a/services/accessibility/java/com/android/server/accessibility/AccessibilityInputFilter.java
+++ b/services/accessibility/java/com/android/server/accessibility/AccessibilityInputFilter.java
@@ -382,7 +382,12 @@ public class AccessibilityInputFilter extends InputFilter implements EventStream
 
     private void onInputEventInternal(InputEvent event, int policyFlags) {
         final int displayId = event.getDisplayId();
+        // Key events go through the KeyboardInterceptor of the default display whatever display
+        // they carry (processKeyEvent): only the other events are dropped for a display that has
+        // no handler. On the Pocket DS the keys carry the focused display, so with the focus on the
+        // bottom screen they skipped every accessibility service (the M button of AYAHome).
         if (mEventHandler.size() == 0 || (Flags.ignoreInputEventsFromDisplayWithoutHandler()
+                && !(event instanceof KeyEvent)
                 && displayId != Display.INVALID_DISPLAY && mEventHandler.get(displayId) == null)) {
             if (DEBUG) Slog.d(TAG, "No mEventHandler for event " + event);
             super.onInputEvent(event, policyFlags);
